Thumbtack Property Damage and Money Back Guarantee Terms and Conditions (Georgia Only)
[Image: Pill Pro]
[Image: Pill Customer]
Last Updated: June 6, 2019 The following Property Damage and Money Back Guarantee Terms and Conditions (the “PD & MB Guarantee Terms”) apply only to requests made from September 6, 2018 to December 31, 2019 (inclusive) for projects in which the zip code input by the Consumer submitting the request is in the State of Georgia. All other requests are subject to the Thumbtack Guarantee and its Terms and Conditions. RELATIONSHIP TO THUMBTACK TERMS OF USE AND PRIVACY POLICY All capitalized terms used but not defined in these PD & MB Guarantee Terms shall have the same meanings as in Thumbtack’s Terms of Use and Privacy Policy. Except as explicitly provided herein, nothing in these PD & MB Guarantee Terms shall be construed to invalidate any part of the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy, which shall remain in full force and effect. IN PARTICULAR, THE THUMBTACK TERMS OF USE CONTAIN A BINDING ARBITRATION PROVISION AND CLASS ACTION WAIVER. IT AFFECTS YOUR LEGAL RIGHTS AS DETAILED IN THE ARBITRATION AND CLASS ACTION WAIVER SECTION. PLEASE READ THE TERMS OF USE CAREFULLY. You acknowledge and agree that by using the Platform, you indicate you have read, and that you understand and agree to be bound by, these PD & MB Guarantee Terms. THE THUMBTACK PROPERTY DAMAGE AND MONEY BACK GUARANTEE The Thumbtack Property Damage and Money Back Guarantee (“PD & MB Guarantee”) includes two parts, each of which are subject to the limitations, exclusions, and conditions of these PD & MB Guarantee Terms, including the Limit:
(1) Property Damage Guarantee: Thumbtack agrees to pay Consumers when a Responsible Service Professional fails to do so to repair or replace Covered Property subject to a Covered Property Loss;
(2) Money Back Guarantee: When a Responsible Service Professional materially deviates from the material terms of the Thumbtack Scope of Work Agreement, if such deviation is not corrected by the Responsible Service Professional within a reasonable time following formal notification of the deficiency from the Consumer, Thumbtack, in its sole discretion, agrees to: (a) Pay the Consumer the total amount paid to the Responsible Service Professional by the Consumer; or(b) Pay the Consumer the amount reasonably required to remedy the material deviation from the Scope of Work Agreement. Some important restrictions to understand are:
Property Damage Guarantee (1) The Property Damage Guarantee is generally limited to One Million United States Dollars, and it applies only to Consumers. This means that losses in excess of these amounts per Incident will not be covered, and Thumbtack will accept reimbursement requests only from the person who, using the Platform as a Consumer requested work and hired the Service Professional through Thumbtack. (2) The Property Damage Guarantee covers direct physical loss or physical damage, which means and is limited to: (a) complete destruction of property, or (b) partial destruction or damage to property, except for minor or cosmetic damage. Faulty installation, incomplete work, or both together do not constitute “direct physical loss or physical damage.” (3) To be covered by the Property Damage Guarantee, Consumers must provide Proof of Hire. This Proof must include the original request on Thumbtack and the quote provided by the Service Professional as well as any one of the following:
(a) On-platform messaging and documentation confirming, as determined in Thumbtack’s sole discretion, that the Consumer agreed to hire the Service Professional for a project.
(b) Off-platform communications between the Consumer and Service Professional confirming, as determined in Thumbtack’s sole discretion, that the Consumer agreed to hire the Service Professional for a project.
(c) A copy of a contract, invoice or other project document agreed to by Service Professional and Consumer demonstrating that the Consumer agreed to hire the Service Professional.
(d) Any other information that Thumbtack, in its sole discretion, determines is sufficient to show a Consumer agreed to hire the Service Professional. This Proof must demonstrate that the Consumer hired the Service Professional no later than 30 days after the Consumer submitted their initial request for Pro Services and prior to work actually commencing.
(4) Losses must be incurred as a direct result of work requested on Thumbtack and must be caused by the negligence of a Service Professional. This means the Property Damage Guarantee covers property damage directly and primarily caused by the negligence of a Service Professional in the course of performing the work requested by the Consumer on the Platform. (5) Thumbtack will first require Consumers to make a good faith attempt to resolve any claims of damages with the Service Professional. Most covered issues can be resolved amicably, and we are here to help. Before the Property Damage Guarantee applies, we will first try to help Consumers resolve problems with Service Professionals directly. (6) Before making a payment under the Property Damage Guarantee, Thumbtack will first require Consumers to obtain payment from any applicable insurance policy or policies, seek and fail to obtain payment from any applicable insurance policy or policies, or certify that no applicable insurance policy exists.
(7) Other conditions apply. Please read this document carefully to understand how the Property Damage Guarantee works. In particular, please review sections addressing Excluded Property, Excluded Losses, and Conditions. Money Back Guarantee (1) The Money Back Guarantee is limited to One Thousand United States Dollars, and it applies only to Consumers. This means that project costs, repair costs, or other costs or losses in excess of these amounts per Project will not be covered, and Thumbtack will accept reimbursement requests only from the person who, using the Platform as a Consumer, requested work and hired the Service Professional through Thumbtack. (2) The Money Back Guarantee covers only the lesser of the total amount paid to the Responsible Service Professional by the Consumer or the amount reasonably required to repair or otherwise remedy the material deviation from the Scope of Work Agreement. (3) To be covered by the Money Back Guarantee, Consumers must provide Proof of Hire. This Proof must include the original request on Thumbtack and the quote provided by the Service Professional as well as any one of the following:
(a) On-platform messaging and documentation confirming, as determined in Thumbtack’s sole discretion, that the Consumer agreed to hire the Service Professional for a project.
(b) Off-platform communications between the Consumer and Service Professional confirming, as determined in Thumbtack’s sole discretion, that the Consumer agreed to hire the Service Professional for a project.
(c) A copy of a contract, invoice or other project document agreed to by Service Professional and Consumer demonstrating that the Consumer agreed to hire the Service Professional.
(d) Any other information that Thumbtack, in its sole discretion, determines is sufficient to show a Consumer agreed to hire the Service Professional. This Proof must demonstrate that the Consumer hired the Service Professional no later than 30 days after the Consumer submitted their initial request for Pro Services and prior to work actually commencing.
(4) The Consumer must have completed a Scope of Work Agreement listing material components of the project prior to any work commencing.
(5) The Money Back Guarantee covers costs for projects scoped through the Thumbtack platform only. This means that add-on projects or other projects outside the bounds of the job originally requested on Thumbtack are not covered. (6) Thumbtack will first require Consumers to make a good faith attempt to resolve any claims of damages with the Service Professional. Most covered issues can be resolved amicably, and we are here to help. Before the Money Back Guarantee applies, we will first try to help Consumers resolve problems with Service Professionals directly. (7) Other conditions apply. Please read this document carefully to understand how the Money Back Guarantee works. In particular, please review sections addressing Excluded Property, Excluded Losses, and Conditions. While the above restrictions are important, you should also review this entire document to understand how the Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee applies to Consumers and how it works. NATURE OF THE THUMBTACK PD & MB GUARANTEE THE THUMBTACK PD & MB GUARANTEE IS NOT INSURANCE. NO USER, CONSUMER, SERVICE PROFESSIONAL, OR OTHER THIRD PARTY IS AN INSURED OR OTHER THIRD PARTY BENEFICIARY UNDER THESE TERMS OR ANY INSURANCE POLICY. TO THE EXTENT ANY SUCH PARTIES DESIRE PROTECTION BEYOND THE SCOPE OF THE THUMBTACK PD & MB GUARANTEE, THEY MUST PURCHASE INSURANCE THAT WILL PROVIDE SUFFICIENT COVERAGE. PLEASE REVIEW THIS DOCUMENT CAREFULLY. CONSUMERS MUST COMPLY WITH ALL OF THE REQUIREMENTS AND CONDITIONS OF THE PD & MB GUARANTEE TERMS TO BE ELIGIBLE TO RECEIVE ANY PAYMENTS. FAILURE TO FULLY COMPLY WILL PREVENT RECOVERY FOR ANY COVERED LOSSES. NO CONSUMER, SERVICE PROFESSIONAL, OR OTHER PERSON, OTHER THAN THE CONSUMER WHO MEETS THE CONDITIONS OF THESE PD & MB GUARANTEE TERMS WITH RESPECT TO THE CORRESPONDING COVERED LOSS, HAS ANY RIGHTS UNDER THESE PD & MB GUARANTEE TERMS OR ANY OTHER MATERIALS OR REPRESENTATIONS REGARDING THE THUMBTACK PD & MB GUARANTEE. THERE ARE NO THIRD PARTY BENEFICIARIES TO THESE PD & MB GUARANTEE TERMS OR ANY OTHER MATERIALS OR REPRESENTATIONS REGARDING THE THUMBTACK PD & MB GUARANTEE. DEFINITIONS In addition to terms defined within the text of these PD & MB Guarantee Terms, the following capitalized terms shall have the following meanings: “Covered Losses” means and is limited to the following:
(a) For the Property Damage Guarantee: Only Covered Property Losses;
(b) For the Money Back Guarantee: The lesser of the total amount paid to the Responsible Service Professional by the Consumer or the amount reasonably required to repair or otherwise remedy the material deviation from the Scope of Work Agreement.
“Covered Property Loss” or “Covered Property Losses” means and is limited to direct physical loss or physical damage incurred to Covered Property as a direct and primary result of the negligence of a Service Professional in providing Pro Services to a Consumer, or to another recipient at the request of a Consumer, in the Territory. It does not include loss or physical damage incurred to property owned, leased or otherwise in the direct care and oversight of the Service Professional or his or her agents, employees, or subcontractors. “Covered Property” means and is limited to real property or personal property located at the fixed site or sites in the Territory where a Service Professional provided Pro Services to a Consumer or to another recipient at the request of a Consumer, or within 100 feet of such site, to the extent of such person’s interest in such property, and excluding all Excluded Property. “Electronic Data,” means films, records, manuscripts, drawings or photographs, data, information, audio or video recordings, files, facts, programs or other materials stored as or on, created or used on, or transmitted to or from, computer software, including systems and applications software, hard or floppy disks, CD-ROMs, tapes, drives, cells, data processing devices, cloud storage, or any other media which are used with electronically-controlled equipment. “Excluded Property” means any of the following:
(1) automobiles or other transportation vehicles or forms; watercraft (including, but not limited to, boats, yachts, jet skis, and similar craft), aircraft, spacecraft, satellites, and drones;
(2) currency, money, precious metal, notes, or securities;
(3) animals;
(4) commercial crops or timber, mines, dams, dikes, and levees;
(5) property in transit;
(6) Fine Arts; and
(7) Electronic Data, other than as provided below.
“Fine Arts,” means paintings, etchings, printed photos, pictures, tapestries, rare or art glass, art glass windows, valuable rugs, statuary, sculptures, antique furniture, antique jewelry, bric-a-brac, porcelains, antique automobiles, coins, stamps, other collectibles, collections, furs, jewelry, precious stones, precious metals, and similar property of rarity and/or historical value. “Fine Arts” also includes exposed films, negatives, records, manuscripts, drawings, and audio or video recordings in other than digital format that would not constitute Electronic Data. “Incident” means all events or occurrences arising from a common nucleus of operative fact. “Limit” means the following:
(a) For the Property Damage Guarantee: One Million United States Dollars (US$1,000,000) on the date of payment by Thumbtack under these PD & MB Guarantee Terms per Incident for Covered Losses;
(b) For the Money Back Guarantee: One Thousand United States Dollars (US$1,000) per Incident for Covered Losses.
“Ordinary Wear and Tear” means the deterioration in condition of property that occurs under normal use and conditions. “Project” is limited to necessary work by a Responsible Service Professional for the Responsible Service Professional to fulfill its duties under the Scope of Work Agreement. “Reimbursement Amount” means the following:
(a) For the Property Damage Guarantee: The lesser of the Repair Value or Replacement Value of a Consumer’s Covered Property as calculated by Thumbtack in its discretion not to exceed the Limit, computed as of the date of the loss and subject to the following: (i) For devices that store Electronic Data, the Reimbursement Amount will be limited to the blank value of the data storage device plus the reasonable cost of copying information from backup or from originals of a previous generation, if any backup exists. The Property Damage Guarantee does not cover Electronic Data, so costs of research, engineering, or restoring or recreating lost information will not be paid.(ii) Any Reimbursement Amount payable under the Property Damage Guarantee will be reduced by the amount already paid by others for all or any portion of a Covered Loss, including but not limited to payments made to Consumers directly by or on behalf of a Service Professional or other source (such as another responsible party).
(b) For the Money Back Guarantee: Covered Losses computed as of the date of the loss not to exceed the Limit. Any Reimbursement Amount payable under the Money Back Guarantee will be reduced by the amount already paid by others for all or any portion of a Covered Loss, including but not limited to payments made to Consumers directly by or on behalf of a Service Professional or other source (such as another responsible party).
“Repair Value” means the amount it would cost to repair damaged or destroyed Covered Property as a result of a Covered Loss, measured on the date of occurrence of such Covered Loss, with material of like kind and quality, with proper deduction for obsolescence and physical depreciation and less any amount already paid or payable by any insurance policies. “Replacement Value” means the amount it would cost to replace damaged or destroyed Covered Property as a result of a Covered Loss, measured on the date of occurrence of such Covered Loss, with material of like kind and quality, with proper deduction for obsolescence and physical depreciation and less any amount already paid or payable by any insurance policies. “Responsible Service Professional” means the following:
(a) For the Property Damage Guarantee: a Service Professional (1) with whom a Consumer directly connected on the Platform, (2) whose negligence is the direct and primary cause of Covered Losses;
(b) For the Money Back Guarantee: a Service Professional (1) with whom a Consumer directly connected on the Platform, (2) who is the direct and primary cause of Covered Losses;
“Scope of Work Agreement” means a written agreement in any form, including but not limited to messaging or email correspondence, entered into by a Consumer and a Responsible Service Professional prior to commencement of any work on a Project that memorializes the material terms of the Project. “Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee Payment Request Form” means Thumbtack’s form to request payment under this Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee. “Territory” means the United States of America, including territories. LIMITATIONS AND EXCLUSIONS The Money Back Guarantee does not pay for losses to property. Neither the Property Damage Guarantee nor the Money Back Guarantee pays for bodily injury. Neither the Money Back Guarantee nor the Property Damage Guarantee pays for losses arising from or in any way related to any of the following (“Excluded Losses”):
(1) losses that are a normal, usual, or natural part of the work undertaken;
(2) Excluded Property;
(3) acts of nature, including, but not limited to, earthquakes and weather-related events; provided that under the Property Damage Guarantee, a loss is not an Excluded Loss if the Service Professional's negligence was the sole and immediate cause of the vulnerability responsible for a weather-related loss to property and the Consumer did not fail to take reasonable steps to remediate the vulnerability prior to the weather-related loss to property;
(4) losses not directly caused by a Service Professional, including but not limited to consequential damages, special damages, interruption of business, opportunity costs, loss of market, loss of use, and losses or damages associated with the unauthorized acquisition of or access to Electronic Data
(5) losses or damages other than straight Repair Value or Replacement Value related to sentimental items such as family heirlooms or photographs;
(6) losses, damages, or deterioration arising from any delay;
(7) theft or other intentional acts and mysterious disappearance, loss, or shortage disclosed on taking inventory, or any unexplained loss of inventory
(8) enforcement of any law or ordinance;
(9) animals, including injuries to animals, veterinary care, boarding, medications, and all other services associated with animals;
(10) identity theft or identity fraud;
(11) losses, damages, costs or expenses of whatsoever nature, directly or indirectly, caused or partially caused by war or terrorism;
(12) lack of electricity, fuel, water, gas, steam, refrigerant, sewerage, telephone or internet services due to external factors;
(13) the following conditions: (a) previous faulty workmanship, material, construction or design from any cause;(b) deterioration, depletion, rust, corrosion or erosion, inherent vice, or latent defect;(c) Ordinary Wear and Tear;(d) damage caused by insects, animals, or vermin (including pets);
(14) losses, damages, costs, or expenses of whatsoever nature directly or indirectly arising out of or relating to mold, mildew, fungus, spores, or other microorganism of any type, nature, or description, including but not limited to any substance whose presence poses an actual or potential threat to human health. This exclusion applies even if there is: (a) any physical loss or damage to Covered Property;(b) any peril or cause covered hereunder, whether or not contributing concurrently or in any sequence;(c) any loss of use, occupancy, or functionality; or(d) any action required, including but not limited to, repair, replacement, removal, cleanup, abatement, disposal, relocation, or steps taken to address medical or legal concerns.
(15) losses, damages, costs, or expenses of any nature directly or indirectly arising out of the consumption, serving or furnishing of alcohol or other controlled substances, even if foreseeable.
(16) losses, damages, costs, or expenses of any nature directly or indirectly arising out of the operation or use of an automobile, including loading and unloading, except for otherwise-covered property damage that occurs on the Consumer’s property to property owned by the Consumer.
(17) losses, damages, costs or expenses of any nature that are incurred or reported more than six months after after the Proof of Hire demonstrates that the Service Professional was hired.
For the Property Damage Guarantee: Losses to property, or losses arising from or in any way related to work undertaken outside the scope of the work specifically provided by the Consumer on the Platform at the time of the job request shall also be an Excluded Loss. For the Money Back Guarantee: Losses arising from or in any way related to work undertaken outside of the Scope of Work Agreement shall also be an Excluded Loss. Failure to perform services paid for by the Consumer and described in the Scope of Work Agreement is not an Excluded Loss, provided that the Limit for any claim where a Service Professional never performs any material work shall be Five Hundred United States Dollars (US$500). CONDITIONS—PROPERTY DAMAGE GUARANTEE IN ORDER TO BE ELIGIBLE TO OBTAIN PAYMENT UNDER THE PROPERTY DAMAGE GUARANTEE, CONSUMERS MUST FULLY COMPLY WITH EACH OF THE FOLLOWING CONDITIONS. FAILURE TO FULLY COMPLY MAY PREVENT RECOVERY OF ANY COVERED LOSSES IN THUMBTACK’S SOLE DISCRETION. IN ALL CASES, THE BURDEN OF PROOF WILL BE UPON CONSUMERS TO DEMONSTRATE THAT THEY HAVE COMPLIED WITH THE FOLLOWING CONDITIONS AND RESPONDED TO REQUESTS FROM THUMBTACK IN A TIMELY AND GOOD-FAITH MANNER, AND THE CONSUMER MUST:
(1) make sure the Proof of Hire demonstrates that the Service Professional was hired no later than 30 days after the Consumer submits their request for Pro Services and prior to work actually commencing;
(2) use reasonable efforts to comply with Thumbtack’s safety guidelines in connection with the work performed by a Service Professional;
(3) determine whether there are any physical losses or damages to any Covered Property and contact Thumbtack Customer Support no later than 14 days after becoming aware of or receiving actual or constructive notice that the losses or damages have occurred or have been incurred, and in no case later than six months after the Proof of Hire demonstrates that the Service Professional was hired;
(4) timely and in good-faith participate in mediation or resolution processes with the Service Professional, as directed by Thumbtack in its sole discretion;
(5) for all Covered Property that is damaged or destroyed due to a violation of law or criminal act or misdemeanor, file a police report listing such Covered Property;
(6) provide to Thumbtack proof of value, cost, damage, and/or ownership of Covered Property in the form of receipts, photographs, videos, documents, or other forms in Thumbtack’s sole discretion no later than 60 days after first contact with Thumbtack Customer Support, unless Thumbtack provides a written extension of such deadline;
(7) obtain payment from any applicable insurance policy or policies and provide proof of such payment to Thumbtack; seek and fail to obtain payment from any applicable insurance policy or policies and provide proof of such failure; or certify that no insurance policy applies;
(8) timely submit of a signed and sworn proof of loss to Thumbtack no later than 60 days after your initial notification of Thumbtack Customer Support of the Covered Loss, which may include: (a) the time, cause, and origin of the Covered Loss, and evidence and proof of such loss in the form of receipts, photographs, videos, documents and other verifiable forms of proof;(b) the ownership, leasehold, or other interest in the Covered Property for which Covered Loss is claimed;(c) the Replacement Value and/or Repair Value of each item of Covered Property (at Thumbtack’s request and discretion), subject in each case to independent verification by Thumbtack;
(9) if requested, provide the original purchase price of such Covered Property, the date such Covered Property was acquired, the condition of such Covered Property;
(10) protect and preserve any damaged Covered Property from further loss or damages;
(11) at such reasonable times and places that may be designated by Thumbtack or a claims administrator, produce for examination and inspection all evidence of loss. However, the right to make inspections, the making of inspections, and any analysis, advice, or inspection report will not constitute an undertaking by Thumbtack or its claims administrator to determine or warrant that damaged Covered Property is safe or healthful. Thumbtack will have no liability to Consumers or any other person because of any inspection or failure to inspect; and
(12) with respect to Covered Property subject to a loan, mortgage or other security interest, you must notify your lender/mortgagee in writing of any loss that exceeds Fifty Thousand United States Dollars (US$50,000), and provide Thumbtack with a copy of such notice. If the lender/mortgagee notifies you that the lender/mortgagee seeks the reimbursement proceeds for the loss, you must notify Thumbtack in writing of the lender/mortgagee’s request and transmit a written copy of said request to Thumbtack, and provide all other information to enable Thumbtack to communicate directly with the lender/mortgagee. If such loss is determined to be a Covered Loss, Thumbtack will pay the loss benefits to the lender/mortgagee up to the value of the loan or mortgage (subject to the exclusions, limitations and conditions herein), and Thumbtack will not pay you unless and until your monetary obligation to the lender/mortgagee has been satisfied. This condition shall apply to the extent of applicable law in your jurisdiction.
The Property Damage Guarantee applies only to work requested on Thumbtack no earlier than July 11, 2016. CONDITIONS—MONEY BACK GUARANTEE IN ORDER TO BE ELIGIBLE TO OBTAIN PAYMENT UNDER THE MONEY BACK GUARANTEE, CONSUMERS MUST FULLY COMPLY WITH EACH OF THE FOLLOWING CONDITIONS. FAILURE TO FULLY COMPLY MAY PREVENT RECOVERY OF ANY COVERED LOSSES IN THUMBTACK’S SOLE DISCRETION. IN ALL CASES, THE BURDEN OF PROOF WILL BE UPON CONSUMERS TO DEMONSTRATE THAT THEY HAVE COMPLIED WITH THE FOLLOWING CONDITIONS AND RESPONDED TO REQUESTS FROM THUMBTACK IN A TIMELY AND GOOD-FAITH MANNER, AND THE CONSUMER MUST:
(1) make sure the Proof of Hire demonstrates that the Service Professional was hired no later than 30 days after the Consumer submits their request for Pro Services and prior to work actually commencing;
(2) use reasonable efforts to comply with Thumbtack’s safety guidelines in connection with the work performed by a Service Professional;
(3) create a Scope of Work Agreement before work begins;
(4) contact Thumbtack Customer Support no later than 14 days after becoming aware of or receiving actual or constructive notice of a material deviation from the material terms of the Scope of Work Agreement, and in no case later than six months after the Proof of Hire demonstrates that the Service Professional was hired;
(5) timely and in good-faith participate in mediation or resolution processes with the Service Professional, as directed by Thumbtack in its sole discretion;
(6) for any claim alleging a violation of law or criminal act or misdemeanor, file a police report covering such claim;
(7) provide to Thumbtack the Scope of Work Agreement and any additional materials, including but not limited to proof of project costs and proof of payment in the form of receipts, photographs, videos, documents, or other forms in Thumbtack’s sole discretion no later than 60 days after first contact with Thumbtack Customer Support, unless Thumbtack provides a written extension of such deadline;
(8) submit a signed and sworn proof of loss to Thumbtack no later than 60 days after your initial notification of Thumbtack Customer Support of the Covered Loss, which may include: (a) the time, cause, and origin of the Covered Loss, and evidence and proof of such loss in the form of receipts, photographs, videos, documents and other verifiable forms of proof;(b) the the amount reasonably required to repair or otherwise remedy the material deviation from the Scope of Work Agreement, subject to independent verification by Thumbtack;(c) the total costs paid to the Responsible Service Professional by the Consumer; and
(9) at such reasonable times and places that may be designated by Thumbtack or a claims administrator, produce for examination and inspection all evidence of incompletion. However, the right to make inspections, the making of inspections, and any analysis, advice, or inspection report will not constitute an undertaking by Thumbtack or its claims administrator to determine or warrant that any property inspected is safe or healthful. Thumbtack will have no liability to Consumers or any other person because of any inspection or failure to inspect.
The Guarantee applies only to work requested on Thumbtack no earlier than September 6, 2018. DISPOSITION OF THUMBTACK PD & MB GUARANTEE PAYMENT REQUEST FORMS Thumbtack will complete its processing of any Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee Payment Request Form within a reasonable period following the date the Consumer has complied with all conditions herein. In any event, Thumbtack will use commercially reasonable efforts to complete processing of any Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee Payment Request Form within one month after our receipt of all necessary documents and supporting information. Thumbtack may use third-party service providers, including a claims administrator, to assist in the processing of the Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee Payment Request Forms, and in the investigation and adjustment of payment requests relating thereto. If a claim is approved, then as a condition to payment, Consumers will be required to execute and deliver to Thumbtack an “Approved Payment Request Agreement,” which includes agreement:
(1) to assign to Thumbtack or its designee any rights and remedies the Consumer may have to recover from any Service Professional that is the subject of the Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee Payment Request Form the amount paid to the Consumer or directly to another person in Thumbtack’s sole discretion;
(2) to reasonably cooperate with Thumbtack or its claims administrator, including, at our request, appearing as a witness in any court, arbitration or like proceeding, if Thumbtack seeks to recover the amount paid from any third party;
(3) to release and hold harmless Thumbtack and its claims administrator and all officers, directors, employees, contractors and agents of Thumbtack from any further liability or obligations with respect to the facts and circumstances of the matters and Incident set forth in the Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee Payment Request Form;
(4) to hold in confidence the facts and circumstances surrounding the request, payment under the PD & MP Guarantee, and any discussions with Thumbtack regarding the facts and circumstances surrounding the request, payment under the PD & MB Guarantee, and application of the Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee; and
(5) to immediately refund to us any amounts that are erroneously paid, with such determination to be made in Thumbtack’s sole discretion.
APPROVED PAYMENT REQUEST If a proper request is approved in whole or in part for a Covered Loss (an “Approved Payment Request”), Consumers will be paid the Reimbursement Amount as calculated by Thumbtack or its claims administrator in their sole discretion. For an Approved Payment Request that involves Covered Losses for Covered Property belonging to a party other than the Consumer, Thumbtack reserves the right, in our sole discretion, but have no obligation, to pay all or a portion of the Reimbursement Amount to the owner of that Covered Property. If a Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee payment for all or a portion of such amount is made directly to the owner of such Covered Property, Consumers agree that such payment will be treated for purpose of the Approved Payment Request as being paid to those Consumers directly, and that they will be solely responsible for collecting from the owner of such Covered Property any portion of such payment to which they believe they are legally entitled. For clarity, (1) Consumers’ indemnification obligations set forth below under the paragraph entitled “Indemnification and Release” will apply to claims arising from any payments made pursuant to the Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee, including without limitation any payments made directly to the owner of any Covered Property and (2) Thumbtack’s reservation of rights to pay amounts to the owner of Covered Property does not give rise to third party beneficiary rights to the recipients of such payments or any other third party. ACKNOWLEDGMENTS AND AGREEMENTS You acknowledge and agree that:
(1) the Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee is a guarantee of obligations of a Service Professional and is dependent upon Consumers timely and in good-faith participation in mediation or resolution processes with the Service Professional, as directed by Thumbtack in its sole discretion;
(2) Thumbtack provides Consumers with the Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee described herein solely for the purpose of building customer loyalty and strengthening customer confidence as to use of the Platform;
(3) these PD & MB Guarantee Terms are not intended to constitute an offer to insure, do not constitute insurance or an insurance contract, and do not take the place of insurance obtained or obtainable by Consumers or any other party. Furthermore, these PD & MB Guarantee Terms are not an insurance service agreement;
(4) the benefits provided under these PD & MB Guarantee Terms are solely as set forth in the paragraph entitled “The Thumbtack Property Damage and Money Back Guarantee” above and such benefits are not assignable or transferable by Consumers or any other party, including without limitation any transfer or assignment by operation of law or in connection with divorce or death;
(5) notwithstanding any Consumer’s delivery of all information and materials required to be provided to Thumbtack in order to comply with the conditions set forth in the paragraph entitled “Conditions,” Thumbtack and/or its claims administrator reserve the right to independently investigate (or to have independently investigated) at our sole discretion and expense, the facts and circumstances of a payment request set forth in any Thumbtack PD & MB Guarantee Payment Request Form filed with Thumbtack, including a review of the background of any person involved in the request;
(6) Thumbtack reserves the right, at any time, to offset or deduct from the amounts payable or paid by Thumbtack under these PD & MB Guarantee Terms, any amounts that it may have in its possession, or to subsequently collect, from any other person or entity who is obligated to compensate for losses or damages;
(7) because these PD & MB Guarantee Terms constitute a guarantee agreement, the theory of exoneration applies. Thus, if the Covered Property in question or the risk associated with that Covered Property changes materially, Thumbtack will be entitled to exoneration with respect to any potential guaranty obligation under these PD & MB Guarantee Terms.
